<h1>Jayden Daniels' Second Dislocated Elbow: <em>A Pattern, Not a Fluke</em></h1>
<div class="meta-row">
<span>📖 5 min read</span>
<span>🏈 Football</span>
<span>⚠️ Commanders · Week 3</span>
</div>
<p class="dek">Jayden Daniels dislocated his left elbow for the second year running in Washington's loss to the Cowboys, the same joint he dislocated in Week 9 of last season. Marcus Mariota starts Week 3 against Seattle while Daniels awaits further imaging. The injury sits on his non-throwing arm — but the explosive, live-arm scrambling that makes Daniels special is exactly what keeps putting that elbow on the ground.</p>
</div><div class="content">
<div class="toc">
<div class="toc-label">In This Article</div>
<a href="#injury">What Happened</a>
<a href="#pattern">Why This Keeps Happening</a>
